{"data": [{"author_id": "18336149", "created_at": "2026-11-11T08:44:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120437379785781250"], "id": "2120437379785781250", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 725, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "6/10 Error correction: qubits are fragile. Heat, vibration, even stray light can flip one — so a quantum computer constantly checks and fixes its own errors.\n\nIt takes hundreds of physical qubits to make one reliable logical qubit. That is the real race.", "url": "https://x.com/senthazalravi/status/2120437379785781250"}, {"author_id": "1886731800560472064", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:45:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120573540013428818"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "10666172", "start": 7, "username": "skdh"}, {"end": 79, "id": "1720665183188922368", "start": 74, "username": "grok"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/tebZf4rjwp", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/joxjeff/status/2120573540013428818/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120573525891158016", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/tebZf4rjwp"}, {"display_url": "x.com/skdh/status/21…", "end": 328, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/skdh/status/2116501691486924961", "start": 305, "url": "https://t.co/PzKoPHNPaf"}]}, "id": "2120573540013428818", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 159, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Sabine @skdh is joking, but the joke points at a real bill, so I'm asking @grok to run the numbers.\n\nA qubit is a hold that leaks. Its quantum state bleeds into the world around it, and the bill is the steady top-up that replaces what leaks, every cycle. Today's machines pay with https://t.co/tebZf4rjwp https://t.co/PzKoPHNPaf", "url": "https://x.com/joxjeff/status/2120573540013428818"}, {"author_id": "253138059", "created_at": "2026-11-11T06:37:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120405422729486812"], "id": "2120405422729486812", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 140, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "TECH IDEA | November 11, 2026\n\nTHE 230-FOLD GAP\n\nOn November 5, IBM, Oak Ridge National Laboratory, and AMD announced infrastructure that sounds dull until you read the numbers. They are putting IBM's most powerful quantum processor, the 120-qubit Nighthawk, in the same facility", "url": "https://x.com/Goeun_6121/status/2120405422729486812"}, {"author_id": "1995641297017946112", "created_at": "2026-11-11T09:07:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120443231120810330"], "id": "2120443231120810330", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 83, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "We need a usp CPU ecm hard driven nuclear cell battery china has to program polymers wool keratin for an iq 1000 system, it takes time terrance toa chinas study of wool already on the go wooltex \n\nAI Mode conversation\n\nYou said: how do you design an iq 1000 computing system in", "url": "https://x.com/JeffreyJam74526/status/2120443231120810330"}, {"author_id": "976853333574144001", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:10:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120549824034492420"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "IBM Quantum Starling aims for fault-tolerant quantum computing by 2029, and new error correction codes could reduce qubit needs tenfold.", "display_url": "ift.tt/OgtMC1v", "end": 238, "expanded_url": "https://ift.tt/OgtMC1v", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120549825817067520/QGAZF4ui?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120549825817067520/QGAZF4ui?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 215, "status": 200, "title": "IBM’s Starling Chip Could Need Ten Times Fewer Qubits For Error Correction", "unwound_url": "http://quantumzeitgeist.com/ibm-starling-chip-need-ten-error/", "url": "https://t.co/6x99bAardC"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/mgbnTe3HU6", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/YouSolidLedger/status/2120549824034492420/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120549821601701888", "start": 239, "url": "https://t.co/mgbnTe3HU6"}]}, "id": "2120549824034492420", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "IBM’s Starling Chip Could Need Ten Times Fewer Qubits For Error Correction \n\nIBM Quantum Starling aims for fault-tolerant quantum computing by 2029, and new error correction codes could reduce qubit needs tenfold.\n\nhttps://t.co/6x99bAardC https://t.co/mgbnTe3HU6", "url": "https://x.com/YouSolidLedger/status/2120549824034492420"}, {"author_id": "2059561350238461954", "created_at": "2026-11-12T13:36:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120873489926160811"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 113, "id": "18219737", "start": 103, "username": "riverlane"}, {"end": 187, "id": "2059561350238461954", "start": 181, "username": "c12qe"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/TsqsiFGDyp", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/c12qe/status/2120873489926160811/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120872732556406785", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/TsqsiFGDyp"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/TsqsiFGDyp", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/c12qe/status/2120873489926160811/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120872732564865024", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/TsqsiFGDyp"}]}, "id": "2120873489926160811", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Quantum Error Correction is becoming a defining challenge for scalable quantum computing.\n\nIn the 2026 @Riverlane Quantum Error Correction report, produced with Nature Partnership, @c12qe's experts share their perspective on two critical factors:\n🔹 QEC cycle times \n🔹Reducing https://t.co/TsqsiFGDyp", "url": "https://x.com/c12qe/status/2120873489926160811"}, {"author_id": "1692398763396997120", "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:25:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120946085170491529"], "id": "2120946085170491529", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AMD took an equity stake in PsiQuantum. CPUs, GPUs, FPGAs and ROCm paired with silicon photonics for fault-tolerant machines. It's an investment and a roadmap. No logical-qubit result yet. More promised at SC26.", "url": "https://x.com/AmericaGetBig/status/2120946085170491529"}, {"author_id": "1263073818957971457", "created_at": "2026-11-12T13:56:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120873708365414790", "2120875063251464551", "2120875572238651889", "2120878430992355773", "2120878816297881745"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/pzlI5O6B1w", "end": 305, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Alice__Bob/status/2120878430992355773/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120873625930608640", "start": 282, "url": "https://t.co/pzlI5O6B1w"}, {"display_url": "x.com/Alice__Bob/sta…", "end": 329, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Alice__Bob/status/2117267975979897232", "start": 306, "url": "https://t.co/Btl6jQV6I3"}]}, "id": "2120878430992355773", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Gartner recently released its first Emerging Market Quadrant for Quantum Computing, and Alice &amp; Bob is recognized as a \"Pioneer\" and one of the most likely to bring disruption to the market 🐈‍⬛\n\nA few points from the report we completely align on.\n\n🔹No qubit technology has won https://t.co/pzlI5O6B1w https://t.co/Btl6jQV6I3", "url": "https://x.com/Alice__Bob/status/2120878430992355773"}, {"author_id": "1263073818957971457", "created_at": "2026-11-12T13:58:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120873708365414790", "2120875063251464551", "2120875572238651889", "2120878430992355773", "2120878816297881745"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/JHPyQ2FCpy", "end": 305, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Alice__Bob/status/2120878816297881745/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120873625930608640", "start": 282, "url": "https://t.co/JHPyQ2FCpy"}, {"display_url": "x.com/Alice__Bob/sta…", "end": 329, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Alice__Bob/status/2117267975979897232", "start": 306, "url": "https://t.co/Btl6jQV6I3"}]}, "id": "2120878816297881745", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 616, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Gartner recently released its first Emerging Market Quadrant for Quantum Computing, and Alice &amp; Bob is recognized as a \"Pioneer\" and one of the most likely to bring disruption to the market 🐈‍⬛\n\nA few points from the report we completely align on.\n\n🔹No qubit technology has won https://t.co/JHPyQ2FCpy https://t.co/Btl6jQV6I3", "url": "https://x.com/Alice__Bob/status/2120878816297881745"}, {"author_id": "1687442525143912449", "created_at": "2026-11-12T11:41:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120844470702747669"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 221, "start": 216, "tag": "NVDA"}], "hashtags": [{"end": 207, "start": 191, "tag": "QuantumMachines"}, {"end": 215, "start": 208, "tag": "NVIDIA"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/S5TX7h3TFv", "end": 311, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2120844470702747669/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120844467850682368", "start": 288, "url": "https://t.co/S5TX7h3TFv"}]}, "id": "2120844470702747669", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 95, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "NVIDIA’s Alice &amp; Bob decodes cat-qubit errors on GPUs with NVQLink\n\nAlice &amp; Bob decoded LDPC-cat codes on GPUs using NVIDIA’s NVQLink, demonstrating scalable error correction—a key…\n\n#QuantumMachines #NVIDIA $NVDA\n\nquantumzeitgeist.​com/quantum-machines-nvidia-alice-bob-decodes/ https://t.co/S5TX7h3TFv", "url": "https://x.com/QuantumStateX/status/2120844470702747669"}, {"author_id": "1570720298", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:28:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120509078829219980"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 4, "start": 0, "tag": "IBM"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/StockSavvyShay…", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/StockSavvyShay/status/2120505943586938976", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/J31AwRiMfV"}]}, "id": "2120509078829219980", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$IBM  is pushing quantum computing closer to commercial relevance. \n\nNighthawk r3’s 520-qubit design and planned 1,040-qubit system in 2027 mark a major scaling milestone. \n\nThe long-term opportunity is significant, but investors should watch execution, error correction, and https://t.co/J31AwRiMfV", "url": "https://x.com/alexsumar9/status/2120509078829219980"}, {"author_id": "1552181895965712385", "created_at": "2026-11-11T23:04:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120653799635468750"], "id": "2120653799635468750", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 71, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Why quantum computing fidelity matters\n\nA quantum computer with more qubits isn’t automatically a better computer.\n\nError rates matter enormously.\n\nHigher fidelity means operations are more likely to produce the intended result.\n\nThat’s why investors should examine qubit quality,", "url": "https://x.com/NoldeaReally/status/2120653799635468750"}, {"author_id": "1720654322621382657", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:43:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120512645132390436"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 244, "start": 227, "tag": "QuantumComputing"}, {"end": 249, "start": 245, "tag": "QEC"}, {"end": 257, "start": 250, "tag": "Python"}, {"end": 265, "start": 258, "tag": "Qiskit"}], "urls": [{"description": "Learn the fundamentals of quantum error correction with Python, in 38 pages. Error types and the depolarizing channel Syndrome extraction with ancilla qubits...", "display_url": "id01t.gumroad.com/l/yqluhb", "end": 225, "expanded_url": "https://id01t.gumroad.com/l/yqluhb", "images": [{"height": 1508, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120512664929501184/K_aflhVH?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1005}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120512664929501184/K_aflhVH?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 202, "status": 200, "title": "QEC Academy Book 1: Quantum Error Correction Fundamentals with Python", "unwound_url": "https://id01t.gumroad.com/l/yqluhb", "url": "https://t.co/LOpx457GI4"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/nYW8rAqCC0", "end": 289, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/DJiD01T/status/2120512645132390436/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120512585581641728", "start": 266, "url": "https://t.co/nYW8rAqCC0"}]}, "id": "2120512645132390436", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Quantum computers only scale if their errors get corrected.\n\nQEC Academy Book 1 teaches quantum error correction from the first qubit to surface codes, with Python you can run. 38 pages, DRM-free PDF.\n\nhttps://t.co/LOpx457GI4\n\n#QuantumComputing #QEC #Python #Qiskit https://t.co/nYW8rAqCC0", "url": "https://x.com/DJiD01T/status/2120512645132390436"}, {"author_id": "1880950985649963008", "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:12:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120489740785025380"], "id": "2120489740785025380", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Oak Ridge, IBM and AMD launched a testbed for quantum error correction, linking the 120-qubit IBM Nighthawk and the Umbra system with AMD Instinct MI355X accelerators.\nIt supports the DOE target of 100 logical qubits running 100,000 complex operations by the end of 2028.\nFor", "url": "https://x.com/Chirkov_BTC/status/2120489740785025380"}, {"author_id": "1941151648589434880", "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:03:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120487570677047600"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 4, "start": 0, "tag": "IBM"}]}, "id": "2120487570677047600", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 593, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$IBM IBM Unveils Next-Generation Quantum Processor, Targets 1,040-Qubit System in 2027\n⠀\n• Nighthawk r3 is designed to execute 10,000 quantum operations across 520 programmable qubits, with plans to connect two processors into a 1,040-qubit system in 2027.\n• Current Nighthawk", "url": "https://x.com/allday_stocks/status/2120487570677047600"}, {"author_id": "1974377077345247232", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:20:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120295472367567181"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 13, "start": 8, "tag": "RGTI"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/EmmanuelInvest…", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/EmmanuelInvest/status/2120262465866854758", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/6O8fJdHlna"}]}, "id": "2120295472367567181", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 179, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "RIGETTI $RGTI — $497 MILLION IN CASH, BUT MANAGEMENT SAYS MEANINGFUL QUANTUM COMMERCIALISATION COULD STILL BE THREE YEARS AWAY.\nI've reviewed Rigetti's Q3 earnings call, and the technology progress is encouraging. But management's comments on commercialisation deserve just as https://t.co/6O8fJdHlna", "url": "https://x.com/EmmanuelInvest/status/2120295472367567181"}, {"author_id": "2053562969238228993", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:21:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120325915246834022"], "id": "2120325915246834022", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "⚡ SNF PULSE\n\n QUANTUM COMPUTING &amp; CAPITAL MARKETS\n\nQUANTUM HARDWARE CLEARED THE TECHNICAL BAR. REVENUE MISSED THE COMMERCIAL ONE.\n\nQuantum computing is making measurable technological progress.\n\nBut the distance between scientific achievement and commercial profitability remains", "url": "https://x.com/SNFuturesLive/status/2120325915246834022"}, {"author_id": "1901176969443885056", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:00:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120547103923441815"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 33, "id": "357312062", "start": 25, "username": "Bitcoin"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/YumoY7iLZ4", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/QuantusNetwork/status/2120547103923441815/video/1", "media_key": "13_2120495954063200256", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/YumoY7iLZ4"}]}, "id": "2120547103923441815", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 3202, "like_count": 34, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Last week in quantum:\n\nA @Bitcoin Core developer floated \"quantum landmines\" to make theft expensive.\n\nCory Fields posted the idea to the bitcoin-dev mailing list on November 4 and labeled it a thought experiment. An owner would prepare in advance by creating a small quantum-safe https://t.co/YumoY7iLZ4", "url": "https://x.com/QuantusNetwork/status/2120547103923441815"}, {"article": {"title": "IBM + AMD + Oak Ridge = ?"}, "author_id": "2119970090493886464", "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:13:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120943110062522470"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2120…", "end": 49, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2120942631551193088", "start": 26, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2120942631551193088", "url": "https://t.co/LKKoemi1Op"}]}, "id": "2120943110062522470", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "IBM + AMD + Oak Ridge = ? https://t.co/LKKoemi1Op", "url": "https://x.com/Intel8669/status/2120943110062522470"}, {"author_id": "1744524835932241920", "created_at": "2026-11-11T20:51:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120620465320255717"], "id": "2120620465320255717", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "IBM is changing how it plans to scale quantum computing — and the shift is revealing.\n\nThe company now plans to offer access in 2027 to a 1,040-qubit system built from two 520-qubit Nighthawk processors, rather than linking nine smaller 120-qubit chips as previously envisioned.", "url": "https://x.com/DataExos/status/2120620465320255717"}, {"author_id": "1626763763918557188", "created_at": "2026-11-11T04:18:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120370472437399805"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 274, "id": "1984251466136301568", "start": 263, "username": "1096361BTC"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/gNXlsoivOg", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Natepeak4/status/2120370472437399805/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120369718997733376", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/gNXlsoivOg"}]}, "id": "2120370472437399805", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Quantum error correction crossed a real threshold recently. Google's Willow chip demonstrated below-threshold error correction for the first time. That's a genuine milestone. It doesn't mean Bitcoin is broken. It means the timeline got a little less theoretical. @1096361BTC https://t.co/gNXlsoivOg", "url": "https://x.com/Natepeak4/status/2120370472437399805"}, {"author_id": "864604226", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:22:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120507454274314430"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 9, "start": 5, "tag": "IBM"}]}, "id": "2120507454274314430", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 43, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "IBM ($IBM) unveiled Quantum Nighthawk r3, designed for 10,000 quantum operations across 520 programmable qubits, with plans to link two processors into a 1,040-qubit system in 2027.\n\n* Next-Gen Processor: Nighthawk r3 will feature 2,034 physical qubits and 10 chip-to-chip", "url": "https://x.com/JohnnyNorthstar/status/2120507454274314430"}, {"author_id": "1970531672765665280", "created_at": "2026-11-12T07:41:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120783956929093969"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/gzarLfwG5x", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TechieUltimatum/status/2120783956929093969/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120783946342666240", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/gzarLfwG5x"}]}, "id": "2120783956929093969", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 473, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "IBM is making a major push toward more powerful quantum computers.\n\nIts next-generation Nighthawk r3 processor is designed to handle much more complex calculations, with plans to cross the 1,000-qubit milestone in 2027.\n\n• 520 programmable qubits: Nighthawk r3 is designed to https://t.co/gzarLfwG5x", "url": "https://x.com/TechieUltimatum/status/2120783956929093969"}, {"author_id": "1997365117579849728", "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:07:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120488632947450222"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 248, "id": "18994444", "start": 244, "username": "IBM"}]}, "id": "2120488632947450222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_cou